            "content": [
              {
                "type": "output_text",
                "text": "I don’t have live news access, so I can’t verify developments after my knowledge cutoff of **June 2024**. As of then, the latest major updates about NASA’s **Mars Perseverance rover** were:\n\n- **Perseverance was still active in Jezero Crater**, studying rocks that may preserve evidence of ancient Martian environments.\n- The rover had been exploring areas related to an ancient river/lake system, including the **delta and crater-margin regions**, where scientists hope to find signs of past habitability.\n- It had collected and sealed many rock-core samples for the planned **Mars Sample Return** campaign.\n- NASA was reassessing the **Mars Sample Return** architecture in 2024 because of cost and schedule concerns.\n- The companion helicopter **Ingenuity** ended its mission in early 2024 after sustaining rotor damage, but it had far exceeded expectations with dozens of flights.\n\nFor the truly latest news, check NASA’s Perseverance mission page or the NASA Mars rover updates feed.",
